SUMMARY: Criteria (a)-(g) are each met as written: tests, mutations and scope all check out.
The FAIL is on the SPEC Problem requirement, which the lead asked me to test (item 4):
"A flip-and-flip-back should leave the saved plan as it was." In the real page the fix
does nothing on the normal path. The first flip's save response OOB-replaces
#whatif-rate-assumptions-card, and that replaces the row element that carries the
data-phase-basis-* record. When the flip back comes after that response lands, the
branch saves "older", exactly as 6bf3839 does. The fix only helps when the user flips
back inside the 500 ms debounce window. The SPEC's own Facts say "each flip is saved",
so the save between flips is the normal case.

